    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d104">

                <pb facs="0182" n="114" xml:id="pg114"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">763.72111/634a</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to President Wilson </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1914-11-12">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">November 12, 1914</hi>.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">My Dear Mr. President</hi>: I enclose an opinion in
                    regard to the sale of Submarines.<anchor n="3" xml:id="d104-f1"/> I fear that we
                    would be “skating on thin ice” if we adopted the rule suggested.</p>
                <p>It may be within the rules of neutrality but I am afraid we could not convince
                    the average citizen there was any difference in allowing a vessel to be
                    completed here and allowing the parts to be made so that a complete vessel could
                    be shipped and the parts assembled in another port.<anchor n="4"
                        xml:id="d104-f2"/>
                </p>
                <p>If you are in doubt about the matter I would like to talk with you before the
                    matter is finally settled, as I think there is danger in this proposition.</p>
                <p>With assurances [etc.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">W. J. Bryan</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d104-f1" n="3" xml:id="d104-f1-content">
                <p>No copy of this enclosure found in Department files.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d104-f2" n="4" xml:id="d104-f2-content">
                <p>For correspondence previously printed concerning the sale of submarines in parts,
                    see <ref target="frus1914Supp#pg_577">
                        <hi rendition="#italic">Foreign Relations</hi>, 1914, supp., p. 577</ref>;
                        <ref target="frus1915Supp#pg_782">
                        <hi rendition="#italic">ibid.</hi>, 1915, supp., pp. 782</ref>–<ref
                        target="frus1915Supp#pg_783">783</ref>.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
